  "description": "The \u0027dss_recipes_cached\u0027 dataset is a comprehensive collection of cached recipes used within a data science platform. Each entry in the dataset represents a unique recipe, identified by a unique \u0027id\u0027 and a \u0027name\u0027, which often matches the \u0027id\u0027. The dataset is designed to facilitate the management and organization of data processing recipes by linking them to specific projects through the \u0027projectKey\u0027. It also categorizes recipes by their \u0027type\u0027, indicating the method of data processing they employ. The dataset includes information about the input and output datasets associated with each recipe, providing insight into the data flow and transformations. Additional metadata is captured in the \u0027tags\u0027 column, while \u0027engine_parameters\u0027 store configuration details for execution engines like Spark or Hive. The \u0027last_modified_user\u0027 column tracks the user who last modified the recipe, and the \u0027url\u0027 column provides a direct link to the recipe within the platform. This dataset is particularly useful for data engineers and scientists who need to manage and audit data processing workflows, ensuring efficient data handling and transformation across projects.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of cached recipes with project links and metadata.",
